791	PPP		Welcome to the first part of your CPD Team Development Programme, which takes place on Thursday 25th October 2012.\r\n\r\nThis email introduces the MiRo questionnaire and explains how to complete it. \r\n\r\nMiRo Behavioural Mode Assessment, to give it its full name, is a tool that will give you an opportunity to develop your self awareness by reflecting on the approaches to work that you prefer. It will also help you individually and as a team to reflect on the implementation of some your organisational values as an organisation, for example 'Communicate in plain language', 'Embrace transparency', 'Cherish integrity, honesty and fairness'. \r\n\r\nTo get started simply click the link below and copy and paste your user name and password into the appropriate boxes. Then just follow the onscreen instructions. \r\n\r\nThe questionnaire will take about 20-30 minutes to complete and a dictionary may be handy. Please submit your questionnaire online by Friday 19th October. This will allow enough time for me to return your MiRo report prior to the CPD workshop.\r\n\r\nDuring your Team Development Programme we will explore the background to MiRo, what it means for you and a team map which will plot each person's outline results (not the detail of the report) onto a team diagram. This will aid the further development of your team as you discover what drives each team member. The detail of your report will not be shared with anyone else, unless you choose to yourself.\r\n\r\nThere is no right or wrong answer just as there is no one perference that is better than an other in the report, and so I encourage you not to dwell too long on the questions but to go with your initial reaction. I also encourage you to be completely honest in your answers, putting down what you are and not what you would like to be. \r\n\r\nIt is my experience that sometimes people ask, "Am I to reflect on my personal or my professional life?" Although in practice there isn't much difference in the outcome for this assessment, I would ask you to think about your professional life as you answer these questions. \r\n\r\nIf you have any questions about the completion of the assessment please give me a call on 384634.\r\n\r\nOn the 25th the day starts at 9:20 at The Community Farm and will finish at 15:30. I have attached a map to this email and can you bring with you addional footwear like boots or old trainers, a waterproof coat and depending on how cold it is (not as cold as January though!)gloves, hat etc.\r\n\r\nKind regards, \r\nMark	1	58548	2012-10-10 07:26:11.053	2012-10-10 07:39:29.732	1	3911	3911	Team Development Programme - MiRo Psychometric	\N	N
