475	SAM 19th August Darlo	Room Booked\r\nAttendance Recieved from Rebecca	We communicated to you not so long ago that we created a 'getting the edge' program where we would be delivering a number of initiatives under this umbrella where the first initiative will be all about looking in the 'MiRo'.\r\n\r\nThe 'MiRo' behavioural workshops have been designed specifically to be used in the modern workplace. It's not a therapeutic tool nor is it intended to save the world. It's designed to help people work better and smarter. It is essentially a way to help you better understand yourself and others. It also gives you the tools to challenge your perceptions, the way you make decisions and engage with others. \r\n\r\nThat means better communication, better team work and better leadership. MiRo can help you to make the most of what you have and it can help teams and organisations make the most of their people.\r\n\r\nI am pleased to announce that you have been invited to a look in the 'MiRo' workshop of which further details will follow shortly. \r\n\r\nTo start this journey, you will need to complete the online questionnaire in order for me to raise the reports we will be using when we get together.\r\n\r\nYour username and password is at the foot of this email - Please look for your off-line slot which Rebecca will be scheduling for you.\r\n\r\nThank you and looking forward to seeing you soon.\r\n\r\nSimon Charlton\r\nTalent Partner\r\nTalent & Development - Sales & Loyalty\r\n07890753707	1	53235	2010-08-11 10:51:17.102	2010-08-11 15:19:23.988	1	4015	4015	Getting the Edge - A look in the 'MiRo'	\N	N
