569	Birmingham City Council Adults & Communities - Andrea Guffick 		As you know we are having a team building session on the 18th January which will help us get to know each-other better and build a future model for our team going forward.  To aid us with this I would like everyone to complete a MiRo Behavioural Profile. This will allow the team to learn more about each-other in a fun and safe manner, build on our strengths and understand our diverse nature. To that end please find below your MiRo logon details.  All you need do is click on the link and follow the online instructions.\r\n\r\nIn order to help celebrate the teams  diverse set of behaviours and attributes we will display everyone’s behaviour graph on a team map during the day. Though the main body of the report you receive will remain confidential to you.  \r\n\r\nMike Fisher from Capita will explain the MiRo profile in more detail on the day.   \r\n\r\nUntil we meet please remember that;\r\n\r\nThere are no right or wrong Modes of Behaviour each one is valid given the individual and the environment.\r\nModes do not relate to skills, ability or knowledge in anyway.\r\nNo Mode is unhealthy unless used to Excess.\r\nAlthough we lead with one particular Mode of Behaviour, through conscious effort we have access to all four Modes.\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions please let me know.\r\n	1	55683	2011-01-11 13:41:20.768	2011-04-06 14:25:17.875	1	4702	4702	Team Building Event	\N	N
