1	Test 01	0	2012-10-23 18:29:45.209	2012-10-23 18:34:16.565	1	7166	7166	40	f	this \r\n\r\nis  \r\n\r\ncommentary
2	Team 1	0	2012-10-24 07:12:36.627	2012-10-24 07:14:41.855	1	7166	7166	40	f	here is some comment
3	PPP	0	2012-10-24 07:13:22.408	2012-10-24 20:49:48.555	1	3911	3911	40	f	It is significant and yet not surprising that there is such a weighting on Organising and Analysing in the Team Map. This indicates a team that in general is rooted in the here and now, that is focused on factual information, is conventional, able to retain detailed information and is both pragmatic, and comfortable with tried and tested ways of doing things. \r\n\r\nGiven the nature of the service that PPP provides this weighting in behaviours is to be expected. The particular areas to watch out for are around the team's ability to work with change, conflict and creativity.\r\n\r\nIt is equally significant however that Stuart as the Director of PPP brings that attributes of a Driver: innovation, desire to win, risk taker and solution focused to name a few. Given both the positional and personal power that Stuart brings to this role, the MiRo Team Map is more balanced that it might at first seem.\r\n\r\n\r\n
