1	1	Help Index Page	<ul>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#1">How can I change my personal details?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#2">How do I set up a new project?</li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#3">How can I buy completed reports?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#4">How do I add and manage candidates in a project? </a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#5">What should I say in my invitation email?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#6">How do I know what’s happening once I have sent emails to the candidates?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#7">One of the candidates says that they have not received the email that I sent, what should I do?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#8">How can I buy completed reports?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li><a href="#9">What do I do once I have bought the report?</a></li>\r\n\r\n<li>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n \r\n\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="1" >How can I change my personal details?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>Once you have logged in to you practitioner account, click on “Edit My Profile” in the right hand menu. Here you can change your user name and password. You can also edit your other details such as your name, address, telephone number and email address. These are the contact details that will appear on the back of your client’s MiRo report.  </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="2" > How do I set up a new project?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>Log in to your account and click on “My MiRo Projects” in the right hand menu. Click “Add Project”  You will be taken to a screen headed “My Project Information”. Here you can give your project a name and make a few notes for your self. You can also create the text of the email that candidates will receive when you send out their log in details. </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="3" > How can I buy completed reports?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p> Log in to your account and click on “My MiRo Projects” in the right hand menu. You will be taken to your projects control panel, click on the project that you wish to manage to go to the project page. Candidates have completed an assessment will be indicated in the status column. Click “Buy Report” for all those that you wish to buy. Your account will be debited accordingly and you will be invoiced at the end of each month. You can keep track of transactions by clicking on the “My Account” button in the right hand column..</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="4" > How do I add and manage candidates in a project?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p> Log in to your account and click on “My Projects” in the right hand menu. You will be taken to your projects control panel, click on the project that you wish to manage to go to the project page. Here you can add and save candidates to the project. You can send out email invitations individually or all together by ticking the check boxes and clicking on “send email”. You can send as many invitations as you like but once someone has completed their assessment you will not be able to send another to that candidate. \r\n\r\nWhen a candidate has completed their assessment you will receive an email informing you that they have done this. Once you have bought the report you can download it as many times as you like. </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="5" > What should I say in my invitation email?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>The information you put in the project email fields is what the candidates will actually see so you need to keep it simple and easy to understand. Some information about how and when they will receive their results is usually helpful and your contact details in case they have any questions. If you need to give them lots of information about an event or training session it is probably best to do that in a different email. Candidates will receive their login details with your message.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="6" > How do I know what’s happening once I have sent emails to the candidates?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>Once you have saved a candidate in a project they will appear in your list of candidates. The status column will indicate “Email Not Sent” until you choose to do so. Once you have sent an email to a candidate “Email Sent” will appear in the status column. Only when the candidate has completed the assessment will this change to “Add to Cart”, you will also receive an email to tell you when each candidate has completed their assessment. </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="7" > One of the candidates says that they have not received the email that I sent, what should I do?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>You might have entered the candidate’s details incorrectly. You can go back to the project screen and edit their details any time you like. You can also resend emails up until the candidate has completed the assessment. If this does not fix the problem it may be that the error is being caused by the candidate’s email server. Some servers like Bigfoot have spam filters which can sometimes interfere with automated email systems like ours. If the candidate does not have another email address that you can use, you can direct the email to yourself and then forward it to your candidate manually. </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="8" > How can I buy completed reports?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>Once candidates have completed their assessment and you have received a notification email, you will see the words “Buy Report” in the status column next to the candidate's name on the project screen. You can select each report that you want to purchase one by one. Each time you will be asked to confirm the purchase. When you do so your account will be charged accordingly, either at the standard rate or at the agreed discounted rate if you have bulk ordered in advance. You can keep track of purchases by clicking on “My Account” in the right hand column. Once you have paid for a report it will appear in the status column next to the relevant candidate’s name, you can then download it as many times as you like. We will invoice you at the end of each month.  </p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h6><a name="9" > What do I do once I have bought the report?</a></h6>\r\n\r\n<p>Once you have paid for a report it will appear in the status column next to the relevant candidate’s name, you can then download it as many times as you like. You can print it off and present it to the candidate at a training session or team build or you can email it to them. If you choose this latter option you must include your contact details in the email and offer them the option of contacting you in order to discuss the report. The report remains the property of the candidate and must not be shown to anyone else without their permission, regardless of who is paying for the project.\r\n\r\nDue to the data protection act we can not hold candidates reports indefinitely and from time to time will delete old reports on the system. We will always tell you before we do this however so you will be able to download and store reports yourself if you want to. However you must not keep personal information about candidates including their MiRo reports longer than is necessary.  </p>\r\n\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>	help
\.
